<p>Use this function to embed a text and background pattern in confidential 
 documents.</p>
<p>If a document with an embedded copy guard pattern is copied, scanned, 
 and/or stored in a machine with the Copy Data Security unit, the image 
 of the page to be printed is destroyed, and replaced with a solid gray 
 image.</p>
<p>Depending on the printer you are using, this function may not be available.</p>
<p class="Note">Note:</p>
<ul>
<li><p>Use the <a href="~/Topics/IDH_HOW_PREVENT"><span class="Term-Soft">Unauthorized 
 Copy Prevention</span></a> function to make the background pattern and 
 text clearly visible when an unauthorized document is copied, scanned, 
 printed, and/or stored in the machine.</p></li>
<li><p>This function requires that the Copy Data Security 
 unit be installed on the printer.<br/>
 Depending on the printer you are using, you may need an MFP that comes 
 with the Copy Data Security unit. For details, see the operating instructions 
 provided with the printer.</p></li>
<li><p>If an unauthorized document is copied, scanned, 
 printed, and/or stored in a machine without the Copy Data Security unit, 
 a warning message will be printed on the printed copy instead of the copy's 
 color being completely gray.</p></li>
<li><p>For details about data security for copying function 
 and effects, see the operating instructions provided with the printer.</p></li>
<li><p>Printing with this function takes longer than 
 normal printing because more data is processed.</p></li>
<li><p>Depending on the data security for copying settings, 
 the driver's prevention pattern may be overwritten by the printer's pattern.</p></li>
</ul>
<ol>
<li><p>Open the printing preferences dialog box after 
 creating a document in an application.</p></li>
<li><p>Click the <span class="Term-Soft">Effects</span> 
 menu on the <span class="Term-Soft">Detailed Settings</span> tab.</p></li>
<li><p>Select the <span class="Term-Soft">Unauthorized 
 Copy Prevention</span> check box.</p></li>
<li><p>Select <span class="Term-Soft">Data Security for 
 Copying</span> in <span class="Term-Soft">Unauthorized Copy Prevention Type</span>.</p></li>
<li><p>Click <span class="Term-Soft">Details...</span> 
 to open the <span class="Term-Soft">Data Security for Copying Details</span> 
 dialog box.</p></li>
<li><p>Select the text type for the prevention text in 
 the list.</p></li>
<li><p>If you select <span class="Term-Soft">User Text</span> 
 in <span class="Term-Soft">Text Type:</span> list, enter a user text using 
 up to 64 single-byte characters.</p></li>
<li><p>To change the font, font style and font size, 
 specify from <span class="Term-Soft">Font:</span>, <span class="Term-Soft">Font 
 Style:</span> and <span class="Term-Soft">Size:</span>.</p></li>
<li><p>To change the angle, specify a value in <span class="Term-Soft">Angle:</span>.</p></li>
<li><p>Select a position to enter the prevention text 
 in <span class="Term-Soft">Position:</span>.</p></li>
<li><p>To repeat text, select the pattern in <span class="Term-Soft">Repeat:</span>.</p></li>
<li><p>Specify the line spacing in <span class="Term-Soft">Line 
 Space:</span>.</p></li>
<li><p>To print the text in outline form, select the 
 <span class="Term-Soft">Outlined</span> check box.</p></li>
<li><p>Click <span class="Term-Soft">OK</span> to close 
 the dialog box.</p></li>
<li><p>After making any other necessary settings, click 
 <span class="Term-OS">OK</span> to close the printing preferences dialog 
 box.</p></li>
<li><p>Start printing.</p></li>
</ol>
